IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — PARTS 16 TO 19: RETURNS, ASSESSMENTS, OBJECTIONS,
-- APPEALS, PAYMENT AND REPAYMENT.
--
-- What must be filed or notified and by when (ss 62-71), records (s 67), when
-- the Comptroller may assess or reassess (ss 72-75), objections and appeals
-- (ss 76-84), when tax is due and what is added if it is late (ss 85, 87),
-- refunds and error relief (ss 93, 93A), and service by post (s 8).
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt lines 843-1264, 29934-32750.

§ `Parts 16 to 19 — process`

§§ `Notices and returns (ss 62, 63)`

-- s 62(4): a chargeable person not required "within 3 months after the
-- commencement of such year of assessment" to make a return must notify the
-- Comptroller "within 14 days after the end of that period". (5): an individual
-- arriving during a YA must notify "within one month of the date of the
-- individual's arrival".
@ref s 62(4)
GIVEN ya IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify chargeability for YA` ya MEANS
    YMD ya 3 31 PLUS 14

@ref s 62(5)
GIVEN `arrived on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a new arrival to notify chargeability, arriving` `arrived on` MEANS
    `add months` `arrived on` 1

-- s 63(1): a person other than an individual that has not made a return must
-- furnish an estimate of chargeable income "within 3 months after the end of the
-- accounting period relating to that year of assessment". (1A), (1B): an
-- individual in business likewise, except for YAs 2026-2030.
@ref s 63(1), (1A), (1B)
GIVEN ya                    IS A NUMBER
      `an individual`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `accounting period ends on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to file an estimate of chargeable income for YA` ya `, individual:` `an individual` `, period ending` `accounting period ends on` MEANS
    IF   `an individual` AND ya AT LEAST 2026 AND ya AT MOST 2030
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`add months` `accounting period ends on` 3)

§§ `Records (s 67)`

-- s 67(1)(a): records kept "for a period of 5 years from the year of assessment
-- to which any income relates". (1)(b): serially numbered receipts where the
-- preceding year's gross receipts exceeded "$18,000 from the sale of goods, or
-- $12,000 from the performance of services".
@ref s 67(1)(a)
GIVEN ya IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last year records must be kept for YA` ya MEANS
    ya PLUS 5

@ref s 67(1)(b)
GIVEN `receipts from goods last year`    IS A NUMBER
      `receipts from services last year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `numbered receipts must be issued, goods` `receipts from goods last year` `, services` `receipts from services last year` IF
    `receipts from goods last year` GREATER THAN 18000 OR `receipts from services last year` GREATER THAN 12000

§§ `Assessments (ss 72-75)`

-- s 74(1): an assessment or additional assessment "within the year of
-- assessment or within ... 4 years (if the year of assessment is 2008 or a
-- subsequent year of assessment) after the expiry of that year of assessment".
-- (2): "at any time" where there has been fraud or wilful default; (2A), (2B):
-- at any time under a mutual agreement or advance pricing arrangement.
@ref s 74(1), (2), (2A)
GIVEN ya                         IS A NUMBER
      d                          IS A DATE
      `fraud or wilful default`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `under a MAP or APA agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Comptroller may still assess YA` ya `on` d `, fraud or wilful default:` `fraud or wilful default` `, MAP or APA:` `under a MAP or APA agreement` IF
        `fraud or wilful default`
    OR  `under a MAP or APA agreement`
    OR  d AT MOST YMD (ya PLUS (IF ya AT LEAST 2008 THEN 4 ELSE 6)) 12 31

-- s 75: an assessment may be waived where the tax "does not exceed $15 or such
-- other amount as the Minister may by order prescribe".
@ref s 75
GIVEN tax IS A NUMBER
      `a prescribed amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Comptroller may waive an assessment of` tax `, prescribed amount` `a prescribed amount` IF
    CONSIDER `a prescribed amount`
    WHEN JUST p  THEN tax AT MOST p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN tax AT MOST 15

§§ `Objections and appeals (ss 76-84)`

-- s 76(3): an objection "must state precisely the grounds" and be made within
-- "(a) if the person is a company and the notice of assessment is served on the
-- person on or after 1 January 2014, 2 months; or (b) in any other case, 30
-- days". (4): extended for absence, sickness or other reasonable cause.
@ref s 76(3), (4)
GIVEN `a company`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `served on`        IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object, a company:` `a company` `, notice served on` `served on` MEANS
    IF   `a company` AND `served on` AT LEAST YMD 2014 1 1
    THEN `add months` `served on` 2
    ELSE `served on` PLUS 30

-- s 79(1): "(a) within 30 days after the date of the Comptroller's refusal to
-- amend the assessment, a notice of appeal; and (b) within 30 days after the
-- date on which the notice of appeal was lodged, a petition of appeal". (3): the
-- notice is deemed withdrawn without a petition. (11): late filing may be
-- permitted for reasonable cause.
DECLARE `Appeal deadlines` HAS
    `notice of appeal by`     IS A DATE
    `petition of appeal by`   IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref s 79(1), (3)
GIVEN `refused on`         IS A DATE
      `notice lodged on`   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `Appeal deadlines`
`the appeal deadlines after a refusal on` `refused on` `, notice lodged on` `notice lodged on` MEANS
    `Appeal deadlines` WITH
        `notice of appeal by`   IS `refused on` PLUS 30
        `petition of appeal by` IS CONSIDER `notice lodged on`
                                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                                   WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (n PLUS 30)

-- s 81(1)-(2): the Board's decision is final, except that where the tax payable
-- (or refund, or notional tax benefit) as determined by the Board "exceeds
-- $200", either side may appeal to the High Court "upon any question of law or of
-- mixed law and fact".
@ref s 81(1), (2)
GIVEN `amount determined by the Board` IS A NUMBER
      `a question of law or mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal from the Board lies, amount` `amount determined by the Board` `, question of law:` `a question of law or mixed law and fact` IF
    `amount determined by the Board` GREATER THAN 200 AND `a question of law or mixed law and fact`

§§ `Payment and late payment (ss 85, 87)`

-- s 85(1): tax is payable "despite any objection or appeal ... within one month
-- after the service of the notice". (2): the Comptroller may extend the time.
@ref s 85(1)
GIVEN `notice served on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay tax assessed by a notice served on` `notice served on` MEANS
    `add months` `notice served on` 1

-- s 87(1): if tax is not paid in time, "(a) a sum equal to 5% of the amount of
-- tax payable is added ...; (b) the Comptroller must serve a demand note ...;
-- (c) ... if the amount of tax outstanding is not paid within 60 days of the
-- imposition of the penalty ..., an additional penalty of 1% of the tax
-- outstanding is payable for each completed month that the tax remains unpaid,
-- but the total additional penalty must not exceed 12% of the amount of tax
-- outstanding". (2): may be remitted for good cause.
-- FORK I7 (as for the carbon tax): the 5% is imposed the day after the last day
-- to pay; completed months run from 60 days after that; the amount outstanding
-- is taken as constant.
DECLARE `Late tax penalty` HAS
    `the 5% penalty`             IS A NUMBER
    `the additional penalty`     IS A NUMBER
    `total`                      IS A NUMBER

@ref s 87(1)
GIVEN outstanding IS A NUMBER
      `last day`  IS A DATE
      `as at`     IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Late tax penalty`
`the late payment penalty on tax of` outstanding `due by` `last day` `, as at` `as at` MEANS
    `Late tax penalty` WITH
        `the 5% penalty`         IS `five`
        `the additional penalty` IS `additional`
        `total`                  IS `five` PLUS `additional`
    WHERE
        `imposed on` MEANS `last day` PLUS 1
        `five` MEANS IF outstanding GREATER THAN 0 AND `as at` AT LEAST `imposed on` THEN outstanding TIMES 5% ELSE 0
        `start` MEANS `imposed on` PLUS 60
        `months` MEANS `count from` 0
        `count from` n MEANS IF `add months` `start` (n PLUS 1) AT MOST `as at` THEN `count from` (n PLUS 1) ELSE n
        `uncapped` MEANS IF outstanding GREATER THAN 0 AND `as at` GREATER THAN `start` THEN outstanding TIMES 1% TIMES `months` ELSE 0
        `additional` MEANS IF `uncapped` GREATER THAN outstanding TIMES 12% THEN outstanding TIMES 12% ELSE `uncapped`

@ref s 87(1)(b)
GIVEN `demand note served on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay a demand note served on` `demand note served on` MEANS
    `add months` `demand note served on` 1

§§ `Refunds and error relief (ss 93, 93A)`

-- s 93(2): a claim for repayment of tax overpaid "must be made within ... 4 years
-- (if the year of assessment to which the claim relates is 2008 or a subsequent
-- year of assessment) from the end of the year of assessment".
-- s 93A(1): relief for an error or mistake in a return, "not later than ... 4
-- years (if the year of assessment within which the assessment is made is 2008
-- or a subsequent year ...) after the end of the year of assessment within which
-- the assessment was made". (1A): for YA 2019 on, a related-party error needs
-- transfer-pricing documentation.
@ref s 93(2)
GIVEN ya          IS A NUMBER
      `claimed on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a repayment claim for YA` ya `made on` `claimed on` `is in time` IF
    `claimed on` AT MOST YMD (ya PLUS (IF ya AT LEAST 2008 THEN 4 ELSE 6)) 12 31

@ref s 93A(1), (1A)
GIVEN `YA in which the assessment was made` IS A NUMBER
      `applied on`                          IS A DATE
      `a related-party error without TP documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `error relief may be applied for, the assessment made in YA` `YA in which the assessment was made` `, applied on` `applied on` `, undocumented related-party error:` `a related-party error without TP documentation` IF
        `applied on` AT MOST YMD (`YA in which the assessment was made` PLUS (IF `YA in which the assessment was made` AT LEAST 2008 THEN 4 ELSE 6)) 12 31
    AND NOT `a related-party error without TP documentation`

§§ `Service by post (s 8(2))`

-- s 8(2): a notice sent by post "is deemed to have been served on the day
-- succeeding the day on which the notice would have been received in the
-- ordinary course of post" (that day is an input).
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN `would be received in the ordinary course of post on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a posted notice is served, ordinarily received on` `would be received in the ordinary course of post on` MEANS
    `would be received in the ordinary course of post on` PLUS 1
